I’m checking the repository’s shipping-gate instructions so I can give you the exact staging command and handoff—without running it.
Use **`$merge --staging`**.

It:

- Rechecks branch protection, staging readiness, the PR, and green CI.
- Merges the feature PR into `staging`.
- Deploys and smoke-tests the staging environment.
- Hands you a plain-language human test script for the deployed staging target.
- Stops so you can test it yourself—it never self-certifies staging.

When you confirm **“Staging works,”** it records a `staging-signoff` pinned to the exact tested commit and provides the run report. That sign-off is required for the later `$merge --production` gate.

Nothing has been shipped.
